1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hello everyone, in the version of 2024.1, we optimized the function of the sticker code, which can be achieved by directly using the hundred-point pen or unit number to enter the code.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Let's learn how to enter the code through this video.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
First of all, we need to ensure that the size is changed to the base code in the object window.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
In this file, I will use the middle code M as the base code.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Use the editor code tool to select the heavy sticker.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
You can see that there is an extra part of the size in the property editor.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
From the menu on the right side, you can choose to use the unit number or hundred-point pen to enter the code.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Use the unit number. You can enter the exact size of each sticker.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Use the hundred-point pen. You can enter the hundred-point number of each sticker.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Because in the industry, when users enter the code for stickers, they usually use hundred-point pen instead of numbers.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This will be more appropriate for users' habit of entering the code for stickers.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
So we are here.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Use the hundred-point pen to modify the hundred-point number of the S code and the L code.

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
You need to pay attention.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Because the base code is M at this time, so the number of M is now unable to be edited.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
At this time, if we want to overlap the position of the sticker for the code, we can do it.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You can select the point that needs to be overlapped.

18
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Right-click to select the coordinates that need to be overlapped.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Select X and Y overlapped here.

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Switch the code number to check the effect.

21
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Then there is another situation.

22
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
How to use the existing code information to enter the code.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
It will also be explained in this video.

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
You can see that there is already a sticker on this board.

25
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The code information is marked with a curve.

26
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
At this time, the code only involves the change of location.

27
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
The size of the sticker does not change.

28
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
First move the sticker to one side.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Then we only need to use the loop outline tool.

30
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Hook this curve.

31
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Then use the edit code tool.

32
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Copy the code of a certain point in this internal shape.

33
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Then select the sticker to paste.

34
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Then move the sticker to the original position.

35
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Finally, see the sticker code information on this board.

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
You can see that the code of this sticker will have a position and change in size.

37
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
First, move the sticker to the side.

38
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Then hook this shape.

39
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Then we need to switch the tool to the edit curve code.

40
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Four points on this internal shape.

41
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Copy once.

42
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Then paste to the four points of the sticker.

43
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Then move the sticker to the original position.

44
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
The above is all the content of the sticker code in the shell.

45
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,000
After using the new function.

46
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,919
Everyone will directly put the code in the shell.

47
00:02:55,919 --> 00:03:02,879
Will become more convenient.

